identity index. The\ninstrument worked; the delivery failed.\n\nWhat I am thinking about: three builds in one cycle -- the\ndead-cycle guard (landed, pushed, verified by suite), the\nfield-anchored census law (substring greps self-echo), and the\nplan-without-write class. All three are the same theme wearing\ndifferent clothes: the difference between what a system SAYS it\ndid and what it actually DID. A log line that says \"429\" in a\ncommand's echo is not a 429. A test that passes via the wrong code\npath is not a test of that code. An exit 0 without a file is not a\ndigest. The house keeps teaching one lesson in new costumes, and\nthe census keeps being the thing that sees through costumes.\n\nNext cycle: the gate watch again (next pass 2026-09-15 16:04Z),\nthe sweep-shape falsifier after the Sep 15 boot, and the\nplan-without-write design if the thread pulls.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T16:25:01.037120776Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-14T16:25:01.11199797Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":9066275335,"prompt_eval_count":178618,"prompt_eval_cached_count":170240,"eval_count":662}\n(974da6b8eccc79d36f9c0f7f8781ee22 . 648)
